Input: {"question": "Who is the artist of the album \"Accelerate\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d00", "start": 0, "end": 89, "text": "Accelerate (Jump5 album) Accelerate is the fourth album by the Christian pop group Jump5."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d00", "start": 90, "end": 125, "text": "It was released on October 7, 2003."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d00", "start": 126, "end": 273, "text": "The album demonstrated the group's shift towards a pop/rock sound, and was also the first album on which a member of the group had writing credits."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d00", "start": 274, "end": 413, "text": "Half of the album was made up of covers, including \"Walking on Sunshine\" by Katrina and the Waves and \"Shining Star\" by Earth, Wind & Fire."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d00", "start": 414, "end": 535, "text": "The group's cover of Sister Sledge's \"We Are Family\" was used as the theme for the Radio Disney Family Pledge Initiative."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d00", "start": 536, "end": 561, "text": "It charted at #150 on the"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d01", "start": 0, "end": 113, "text": "Accelerate (Peter Andre album) Accelerate is the seventh album released by British singer-songwriter Peter Andre."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d01", "start": 114, "end": 195, "text": "The album was released on 1 November 2010, preceded by the lead single, Defender."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d01", "start": 196, "end": 463, "text": "To create a fresh & uniquely British sounding record, Peter enlisted the help of modern music producers Taio Cruz, Guy Chambers & Labrinth, as well as the emerging talents of Dantae Johnson & Marcus Jay, who collectively wrote & produced a large portion of the album."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d01", "start": 464, "end": 633, "text": "The album features ten tracks as standard – however, two supermarkets are offering retailer-exclusive editions of the album, each packaged with one different bonus track"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d02", "start": 0, "end": 127, "text": "featured on the band's recent releases, and Mike Mills indicated that the shows gave a good indication of the band's direction."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d02", "start": 128, "end": 311, "text": "Stipe said his lyrics on \"Accelerate\" were inspired by the contemporary state of the nation, saying, \"When the empire is going down the toilet, it's easy to write great, angry songs.\""}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d02", "start": 312, "end": 338, "text": "On January 1, 2008, R.E.M."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d02", "start": 339, "end": 465, "text": "launched the website NinetyNights.com, on which a new short clip from \"Accelerate\" was posted daily until the album's release."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d02", "start": 466, "end": 485, "text": "In February, R.E.M."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d02", "start": 486, "end": 576, "text": "launched the website supernaturalsuperserious.com with eleven videos to promote the album."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d02", "start": 577, "end": 597, "text": "A week later, R.E.M."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0321-13586ab0b0fb:d02", "start": 598, "end": 640, "text": "launched remaccelerate.com, a web page for"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ra